BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Makar Sankranti / मकर संक्रांति
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270116
DTSTAMP:20261103T045158Z
UID:makar_sankranti-2027-01-15@dharmasetu
CATEGORIES:festivals\,sankranti\,birth-auspicious
DESCRIPTION:Why: solar astronomy made visible as a festival of harvest\, c
 harity (daan)\, and sesame–jaggery offerings to Surya.\n\nStory: Makar S
 ankranti marks the Sun's sidereal ingress into Makara (Capricorn)\, tradit
 ionally linked with Uttarayana — the northward turn of the solar path.\n
 Source: Surya Siddhanta\; Puranic Uttarayana lore\nWhy: solar astronomy ma
 de visible as a festival of harvest\, charity (daan)\, and sesame–jagger
 y offerings to Surya.\nModern angle: Corresponds to a real solar-longitude
  event (sidereal Capricorn ingress). Seasonal marker near mid-winter in th
 e northern hemisphere.\nEvidence: Established\nLink: https://www.drikpanch
 ang.com/sankranti/makar-sankranti-date-time.html\nMore: https://saumya-sha
 rma.github.io/dharmasetu/prototype/reasoning.html#sankranti-solar-ingress
 \nLocation basis: New Delhi. City-specific timing coming later.
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India (reference)
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/prototype/calendar.html#350
 fff9e725b595c
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vasant Panchami / वसंत पंचमी
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270212
DTSTAMP:20261103T045158Z
UID:vasant_panchami-2027-02-11@dharmasetu
CATEGORIES:festivals\,birth-auspicious
DESCRIPTION:Why: mark the turn toward longer light and dedicate the season
  of growth to speech\, learning and the arts.\n\nStory: Vasant Panchami ho
 nours Saraswati on Magha Shukla Panchami\, when spring (vasanta) begins to
  show and learning\, music and yellow mustard fields are celebrated.\nSour
 ce: Puranic Saraswati lore\; regional Grihya customs\nWhy: mark the turn t
 oward longer light and dedicate the season of growth to speech\, learning 
 and the arts.\nModern angle: Seasonal / cultural marker. No clinical outco
 me claim\; supports community learning rituals.\nEvidence: Cultural/psycho
 logical\nMore: https://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/prototype/reason
 ing.html#calendar-lunisolar\nLocation basis: New Delhi. City-specific timi
 ng coming later.
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India (reference)
