BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maha Shivaratri / महा शिवरात्रि
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270306
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270307
DTSTAMP:20261103T045158Z
UID:maha_shivaratri-2027-03-07@dharmasetu
CATEGORIES:festivals
DESCRIPTION:Why: a night vigil of remembrance and restraint at the dark fo
 rtnight's edge\, traditionally linked to Shiva's cosmic dance and marriage
  lore.\n\nStory: Maha Shivaratri is the great night of Shiva\, observed on
  the Krishna Chaturdashi before Magha/Phalguna amavasya — vigil\, fastin
 g and bilva offerings.\nSource: Shiva Purana\; Linga Purana\nWhy: a night 
 vigil of remembrance and restraint at the dark fortnight's edge\, traditio
 nally linked to Shiva's cosmic dance and marriage lore.\nModern angle: Nig
 ht-vigil fasting overlaps with researched intermittent-fasting windows\; e
 vidence for specific Shivaratri outcomes is cultural\, not clinical.\nEvid
 ence: Cultural/psychological\nLink: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/407013
 47/\nMore: https://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/prototype/reasoning.
 html#ekadashi-fasting\nLocation basis: New Delhi. City-specific timing com
 ing later.
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India (reference)
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/prototype/calendar.html#d4b
 c3131946f24fc
