DESCRIPTION:Why: a day set aside to start what should endure — learning
 \, giving\, household foundations — under the spring sun.\n\nStory: Aksh
 aya Tritiya (Vaishakha Shukla Tritiya) is called 'never-diminishing' — t
 raditionally favoured for beginnings\, charity and lasting vows.\nSource: 
 Puranic akshaya lore\; regional muhurat custom\nWhy: a day set aside to st
 art what should endure — learning\, giving\, household foundations — u
 nder the spring sun.\nModern angle: Muhurat timing itself is cultural\; ch
 arity and intentional starts have known psychological benefits.\nEvidence:
  Cultural/psychological\nMore: https://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/
 prototype/reasoning.html#muhurat-cultural\nLocation basis: New Delhi. City
 -specific timing coming later.
