DESCRIPTION:Why: pause at the full moon of Ashadha to name gratitude for t
 hose who taught you how to see.\n\nStory: Guru Purnima (Ashadha Purnima) h
 onours the teacher — traditionally Vyasa\, and by extension every guide 
 who transmits knowledge.\nSource: Skanda Purana / Vyasa Puja tradition\nWh
 y: pause at the full moon of Ashadha to name gratitude for those who taugh
 t you how to see.\nModern angle: Gratitude practices show measurable well-
 being links in psychology research\; the lunar date is cultural.\nEvidence
 : Plausible\nLink: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12585811/\nMore: https:
 //saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/prototype/reasoning.html#calendar-lun
