DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270825
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270826
DTSTAMP:20261103T045158Z
UID:janmashtami-2027-09-23@dharmasetu
CATEGORIES:festivals
DESCRIPTION:Why: stay awake into the night to welcome a story of divine ca
 re arriving in fragile human form.\n\nStory: Janmashtami marks Krishna's b
 irth at midnight on Krishna Ashtami of Bhadrapada (amanta) — the Gokula 
 narrative of protection amid danger.\nSource: Bhagavata Purana Canto 10\nW
 hy: stay awake into the night to welcome a story of divine care arriving i
 n fragile human form.\nModern angle: Night vigil and fasting are cultural-
 devotional\; community singing supports belonging.\nEvidence: Cultural/psy
 chological\nMore: https://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/prototype/rea
 soning.html#calendar-lunisolar\nLocation basis: New Delhi. City-specific t
 iming coming later.
